{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1358159-what-s-a-realistic-reaction-to-superheroes","id":1358159,"title":"What's a realistic reaction to superheroes?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","Additional Discussion","Off-Topic"],"posts":[{"date":"2020-01-01T01:39:48-08:00","id":1358159,"title":"What's a realistic reaction to superheroes?","content":"Like, say, a gigantic portal opens up in the Indian ocean today. It's somehow breaching both the air and the water... yet nothing seeps through. Its like there's a filter letting only solid objects through (the water currents don't intemix). And then, bunch of flying people go through.<br /> <br /> It's the justice league (From Justice league unlimited). Slightly different here, more international and all. But still, it's them. Really recognizably them. So they come up to us, saying that a mad scientist had been planning to invade a defenseless earth with no superheroes to fight off his legions of clones and robots. So we're saved! Only that the portal's kinda permanent. They're working on it, but it'll take a year for the dimensional perturbations to stabilize enough such that they can even begin trying to close it. <br /> <br /> So how would our world react?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12952-accelerator","name":"Accelerator","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-01T04:01:25-08:00","id":1358175,"title":"","content":"Stupidly.<br /> <br /> But hopefully the heroes would, you know, do something about climate change, or some other big issues before closing the portal.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-01T08:47:51-08:00","id":1358202,"title":"","content":"Yeah, really bad reactions all around. They would have been smartest to just lay low and not mention it, doing a public announcement would be like handing a world-changing truth to a bunch of people who react poorly to having their view of the world changed. We'd also wage war with each other over control of the portal. And blame them for it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 01-01-2020, 11:51 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-01T08:59:44-08:00","id":1358203,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1358159-what-s-a-realistic-reaction-to-superheroes?p=1358202#post1358202\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeah, really bad reactions all around. They would have been smartest to just lay low and not mention it, doing a public announcement would be like handing a world-changing truth to a bunch of people who react poorly to having their view of the world changed. We'd also wage war with each other over control of the portal. And blame them for it.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's literally a giant portal it can't be hidden, and it's already seen on the internet","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12952-accelerator","name":"Accelerator","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-01T09:20:38-08:00","id":1358207,"title":"","content":"It's a portal to more resources. Anyone who gains control of it (and nearby you have India, China, the Middle East, and Australia) is basically going to become tremendously rich and get rid of a lot of serious modern day problems.<br /> <br /> It's not something they have to put in a box and take to a fortress. Just like an island, it's something they can claim control of.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-01T09:26:10-08:00","id":1358208,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1358159-what-s-a-realistic-reaction-to-superheroes?p=1358207#post1358207\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's a portal to more resources. Anyone who gains control of it (and nearby you have India, China, the Middle East, and Australia) is basically going to become tremendously rich and get rid of a lot of serious modern day problems.<br /> <br /> It's not something they have to put in a box and take to a fortress. Just like an island, it's something they can claim control of.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's a gigantic bottleneck to an already occupied world with technology likely more advanced than us, with an army of superhumans living inside.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12952-accelerator","name":"Accelerator","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-01T09:35:18-08:00","id":1358210,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Accelerator</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1358159-what-s-a-realistic-reaction-to-superheroes?p=1358208#post1358208\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's a gigantic bottleneck to an already occupied world with technology likely more advanced than us, with an army of superhumans living inside.</div> </div> </div> </div>That will be for whoever crosses it to figure out for themselves. Our governments are not omniscient, they know there's a portal, and aren't going to trust the word of people claiming to be superheroes.<br /> <br /> Even without crossing it, material waste, like hazardous materials we just bury in other countries right now, can be solved without having to personally cross through. <br /> <br /> But a technologically advanced world on the other side is just more of a reward for whoever claims the portal.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 01-01-2020, 12:40 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-01T16:58:54-08:00","id":1358306,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1358159-what-s-a-realistic-reaction-to-superheroes?p=1358210#post1358210\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> That will be for whoever crosses it to figure out for themselves. Our governments are not omniscient, they know there's a portal, and aren't going to trust the word of people claiming to be superheroes.<br /> <br /> Even without crossing it, material waste, like hazardous materials we just bury in other countries right now, can be solved without having to personally cross through.<br /> <br /> But a technologically advanced world on the other side is just more of a reward for whoever claims the portal.</div> </div> </div> </div>*raises eyebrow* <br /> <br /> A person is there. He looks like superman. He flies like superman. He has superstrength like superman. And... you're going to attack? I mean, at the very least, you know that there's some freaky shit going on on the other side of the portal. Bumrushing in to do shit like dumping nuclear waste or invasion seems like really fucking dumb thing to do.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12952-accelerator","name":"Accelerator","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-01T18:01:41-08:00","id":1358315,"title":"","content":"Would I (or likely nofather) attack?<br /> <br /> No.<br /> <br /> Would somebody?<br /> <br /> Probably.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-01T18:14:24-08:00","id":1358317,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1358159-what-s-a-realistic-reaction-to-superheroes?p=1358315#post1358315\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Would I (or likely nofather) attack?<br /> <br /> No.<br /> <br /> Would somebody?<br /> <br /> Probably.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes. But who? <br /> <br /> ....America?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12952-accelerator","name":"Accelerator","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-01T19:54:40-08:00","id":1358335,"title":"","content":"I think a relatively realistic reaction to the revelation that the world depicted in Justice League Unlimited actually exists, exactly as depicted by the show, would probably be an attempt by TimeWarner to revive the show and write episodes where Supes flies through the new portal with free gold for their board of directors.<br /> <br /> Or possibly, on the other side of the portal, the superheroes realizing that everything bad that ever happened to them in their lives, their very existence, was something we wrote to entertain ourselves, and having some sort of mental breakdown.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":177,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","user":"TheCountAlucard","date":". 01-01-2020, 11:08 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-01T20:35:15-08:00","id":1358343,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Accelerator</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1358159-what-s-a-realistic-reaction-to-superheroes?p=1358306#post1358306\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">*raises eyebrow*<br /> <br /> A person is there. He looks like superman. He flies like superman. He has superstrength like superman. And... you're going to attack? I mean, at the very least, you know that there's some freaky shit going on on the other side of the portal. Bumrushing in to do shit like dumping nuclear waste or invasion seems like really fucking dumb thing to do.</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> But who?<br /> <br /> \u2026America? </div> </div> </div>Anyone who wanted, or didn't like someone else getting. Whether that's resources, technology, or simply 'space.' China's building islands solely so they can claim more territory while spying freely on every technologically advanced country as it is, why would they stop? The wealthiest and most powerful organizations in the world all want more.<br /> <br /> Governments make decisions that a sane or reasonable individual wouldn't make. You don't even need a government to do it, just get some people together. Literally as you started this thread there was an attack on an American embassy in Baghdad, a city American forces has bombed hundreds of times and not even that long ago (as old as Vampire the Masquerade). There's a lot of history there but America is far from the only country that would do something aggressive about something as hugely significant as a portal.<br /> <br /> I don't think it would lead to any world peace. I'd go crazy, I love DC Comics, I have a Batman symbol on my wedding ring. And 'realistically' if you played them straight, the Justice League would know better than to just make a public appearance like that, with Martian Manhunter and Aquaman perhaps shooing ships away while some stealth technology was used to shield the portal from view, or just block it. But this isn't the world of comics, if it was we wouldn't need comics to inspire us.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-01T23:36:08-08:00","id":1358360,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Accelerator</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1358159-what-s-a-realistic-reaction-to-superheroes?p=1358306#post1358306\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Bumrushing in to do shit like dumping nuclear waste or invasion seems like really fucking dumb thing to do.</div> </div> </div> </div>And if you think &quot;it would be a dumb thing to do&quot; would stop humans - any humans at all - you obviously need to bone up on your history and/or current events.<br /> <br /> People have been doing patently absurd things for all of recorded history, and it's safe to assume we were making moronic decisions long before then, too. To take just one example from history off the top of my head, see the search for <a href=\"https://youtu.be/UHzkGueRz3g\" target=\"_blank\">El Dorado</a>.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://archiveofourown.org/works/6956863/chapters/15862327\" target=\"_blank\">Magestuck: The Ascension</a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6156-bluecho","name":"Bluecho","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3871"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-02T00:05:45-08:00","id":1358364,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Bluecho</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1358159-what-s-a-realistic-reaction-to-superheroes?p=1358360#post1358360\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And if you think &quot;it would be a dumb thing to do&quot; would stop humans - any humans at all - you obviously need to bone up on your history and/or current events.<br /> <br /> People have been doing patently absurd things for all of recorded history, and it's safe to assume we were making moronic decisions long before then, too. To take just one example from history off the top of my head, see the search for <a href=\"https://youtu.be/UHzkGueRz3g\" target=\"_blank\">El Dorado</a>.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, but in this case, the 'dumb thing to do' would serve to get immediate reprisals. Either with Aquaman sinking the ships doing the shit, Superman stopping them, or Green Lantern just grabbing the nuclear waste and giving it back.<br /> <br /> edit: Humans can do a lot of stupid shit. But when the stupid shit involves getting kicked in the nads by superhumans, that might change.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12952,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12952-accelerator","user":"Accelerator","date":". 01-02-2020, 03:09 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12952-accelerator","name":"Accelerator","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-02T00:33:05-08:00","id":1358368,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Accelerator</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1358159-what-s-a-realistic-reaction-to-superheroes?p=1358364#post1358364\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yes, but in this case, the 'dumb thing to do' would serve to get immediate reprisals. Either with Aquaman sinking the ships doing the shit, Superman stopping them, or Green Lantern just grabbing the nuclear waste and giving it back.<br /> <br /> edit: Humans can do a lot of stupid shit. But when the stupid shit involves getting kicked in the nads by superhumans, that might change.</div> </div> </div> </div>Again, you underestimate the stupidity of the human race.<br /> <br /> OF COURSE it would be a terrible idea. People - especially governments, who are accustomed to vastly overestimating their ability to impose their will on the world - <b>would still do it</b>. Especially if there's even the chance of profit should the plan work.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://archiveofourown.org/works/6956863/chapters/15862327\" target=\"_blank\">Magestuck: The Ascension</a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6156-bluecho","name":"Bluecho","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3871"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-02T02:36:07-08:00","id":1358381,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Bluecho</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1358159-what-s-a-realistic-reaction-to-superheroes?p=1358368#post1358368\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Again, you underestimate the stupidity of the human race.<br /> <br /> OF COURSE it would be a terrible idea. People - especially governments, who are accustomed to vastly overestimating their ability to impose their will on the world - <b>would still do it</b>. Especially if there's even the chance of profit should the plan work.</div> </div> </div> </div>So what happens after the first 20 shattered tankers?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12952-accelerator","name":"Accelerator","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-02T03:08:56-08:00","id":1358385,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Accelerator</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1358159-what-s-a-realistic-reaction-to-superheroes?p=1358381#post1358381\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> So what happens after the first 20 shattered tankers?</div> </div> </div> </div><a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Sunk_cost\" target=\"_blank\">Sunk Cost</a> would kick in, and governments would insist on deepening their investment in the effort, to &quot;make the losses worth it&quot;. Again, if these portals promise any sort of profit - including land, resources, technology, etc. - the allure will never go away.<br /> <br /> Some will naturally give up on the project as a lost cause. <b>That does not mean others won't double down</b>. Like I said, people are capable of incredible stupidity. Whether it's the desire for profit, the fear of someone else having the advantage, or stubborn pride, some people will not let it go.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://archiveofourown.org/works/6956863/chapters/15862327\" target=\"_blank\">Magestuck: The Ascension</a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6156-bluecho","name":"Bluecho","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3871"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-02T03:15:36-08:00","id":1358387,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Bluecho</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1358159-what-s-a-realistic-reaction-to-superheroes?p=1358385#post1358385\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><a href=\"https://&amp;quot;&#91;url\" target=\"_blank\">https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Sunk_cost&amp;quot;]Sunk</a> Cost[/URL] would kick in, and governments would insist on deepening their investment in the effort, to &amp;quot;make the losses worth it&amp;quot;. Again, if these portals promise any sort of profit - including land, resources, technology, etc. - the allure will never go away.<br /> <br /> Some will naturally give up on the project as a lost cause. <b>That does not mean others won't double down</b>. Like I said, people are capable of incredible stupidity. Whether it's the desire for profit, the fear of someone else having the advantage, or stubborn pride, some people will not let it go.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, but sooner or later, someones going to run out of money. I mean, you don't even need superman. Just have someone fire missiles down at the invading ships and blow them to pieces.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12952-accelerator","name":"Accelerator","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-02T03:44:33-08:00","id":1358389,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Accelerator</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1358159-what-s-a-realistic-reaction-to-superheroes?p=1358387#post1358387\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Yes, but sooner or later, someones going to run out of money. I mean, you don't even need superman. Just have someone fire missiles down at the invading ships and blow them to pieces.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes. I know. I keep agreeing, because it IS stupid.<br /> <br /> Stupid, by nature of definition, <i>does not make sense</i>. That's why it's stupid.<br /> <br /> I will totally believe that one nation state or another would grind themselves against a problem until they've depleted themselves, when the more prudent choice would be to do anything else. Because history has given us plenty of examples of people doing exactly that.<br /> <br /> You keep arguing &quot;surely people couldn't be THAT dumb&quot;. I keep retorting &quot;they emphatically CAN be that dumb, and have been for thousands of years&quot;.<br /> <br /> As we speak, there are educated adults who sincerely believe the world is flat. There is a concerted effort by corporations to stop any attempt to combat the climate change that will kill us all, including the people who run those corporations. Donald Trump has occupied the White House for three years, and <i>no one has stopped him yet</i>. I no longer have any illusions about the depths to which human stupidity can sink.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://archiveofourown.org/works/6956863/chapters/15862327\" target=\"_blank\">Magestuck: The Ascension</a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6156-bluecho","name":"Bluecho","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3871"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-02T06:12:55-08:00","id":1358402,"title":"","content":"You clearly wanted some specific answer so why don't you just tell us what you hope would happen.<br /> <br /> As it is now you have the Justice League running around in another planet destroying ships and killing people so their characterization is already wrecked. Unless they came here to conquer, this is not their world and they don't get to make the rules here. The desire to talk to an alternate Earth wouldn't solely be on this side of things, and it's not as if the entire Justice League is accepted by even the society in Justice League's depiction. They were stymied and conspired against at every angle. So is your version of the Justice League just mercilessly slaughtering any human who dares to try and use a portal connecting their two worlds? For a potentially indefinite amount of time until the portal is shut down if that's even possible?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-02T07:38:18-08:00","id":1358416,"title":"","content":"So let me get this straight. Your version of the justice league would just stand there and let people from another world just go up and dump nuclear waste and industrial poisons into their own native Oceans.<br /> <br /> You think them stopping this, is out of character? You think them stopping a suicidal army of human lemmings who attack them for no reason is them being blood thirsty? <br /> <br /> Interesting","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12952-accelerator","name":"Accelerator","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-02T08:36:35-08:00","id":1358421,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Accelerator</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1358159-what-s-a-realistic-reaction-to-superheroes?p=1358416#post1358416\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You think them stopping this, is out of character?</div> </div> </div> </div>Did you know that it's possible to stop a person from doing a thing without necessarily killing them? It's actually <i>more</i> possible, if the person trying to stop them possesses an array of powers that gives them an advantage over the person they're trying to stop.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-02T09:50:02-08:00","id":1358433,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Accelerator</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1358159-what-s-a-realistic-reaction-to-superheroes?p=1358416#post1358416\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So let me get this straight. Your version of the justice league would just stand there and let people from another world just go up and dump nuclear waste and industrial poisons into their own native Oceans.<br /> <br /> You think them stopping this, is out of character? You think them stopping a suicidal army of human lemmings who attack them for no reason is them being blood thirsty?<br /> <br /> Interesting</div> </div> </div> </div>I gave you a list of reasons governments would want access to the portal. You're the one turning the Justice League into a meatgrinder and being disingenuous in every response as well as ignoring much of human (and comic) history.<br /> <br /> Again, if you have some vision of what you think would happen, feel free to post it. But posting the equivalent of 'Psh, really? Uh huh' to every response is just trolling.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 01-02-2020, 12:52 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-02T17:01:53-08:00","id":1358501,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1358159-what-s-a-realistic-reaction-to-superheroes?p=1358433#post1358433\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I gave you a list of reasons governments would want access to the portal. You're the one turning the Justice League into a meatgrinder and being disingenuous in every response as well as ignoring much of human (and comic) history.<br /> <br /> Again, if you have some vision of what you think would happen, feel free to post it. But posting the equivalent of 'Psh, really? Uh huh' to every response is just trolling.</div> </div> </div> </div>Alright, fine. I'll do that for you. <br /> <br /> Forgive me if you don't like it. <br /> <br /> Portal opens. <br /> <br /> Nations of the world go 'oooh'. The 'ooh' turns louder after flying men are seen. The justice league are a bit perplexed by the comics and animated series that shows them so well, but they've seen weirder things. They hold up their hands, and tell us that yes, we're not allowed to go through, sorry for the trouble caused, and yeah, they'll close it in a year or so. <br /> <br /> The nations of the world are really interested, and start reaching out, only to be rebuffed by the justice league. They're busy, they say, and so they aren't going to talk to them. Something something darkseid. The DCAU unlimited series is a hit there, but not much else. Then some bright spark gets the bright idea to invade. Hell, they have superheroes there, and tech at least a decade ahead of us! I mean, yeah, its probably suicidal, but we can invade and try to take their resources. Even if they don't get the resources, they can just dump nuclear and toxic waste there. Surely nothing can go wrong. <br /> <br /> The Justice League start telling the trespassing ships that this is a restricted area, that it is dangerous. The ships do what ships do, and simply start moving faster. Then they stop. Its superman, and he drags the ship back, using a tow chain or just bodily lifting it out of the water, and moving it back into a port. Then he rips out the engine and steering, making it inoperarable. <br /> <br /> This does not deter the other nations in any way, since as you say, they're dumb. So this goes on over and over again. Some of them actually decide to dump the nuclear rods right after they cross the portal. This pisses off aquaman, and he uses his hydrokinesis to just dump them back into our world. All this while, superman or some other superhero is stopping the ships, and then crippling them so that they can't do this shit again. But as you say, they're stupid, and there are a lot of shit. <br /> <br /> After some shit goes down due to superman being too busy to stop the suicidal lemmings, the governments of the JL side decide they've had enough. The JL cannot be too busy spending their time stopping idiots from trying to dump waste or futile attempts to invade them. And so, they say to leave it to them. <br /> <br /> JL asks them how they're going to non-lethally stop them from moving through. The government simply answers that they aren't going to be non-lethal. They're the government, and these are trespassers. The next ship from our world that tries to move through the blockade and dump their waste in the JL world gets blown to pieces. Everybody on board dies. And the government puts out a message, saying that anyone moving through without a permit is to be stopped via lethal force. The governments double down, because as you said, they're stupid and sunk cost fallacy means that they're not going to stop. They make some mouth noises against aggression and attack. <br /> <br /> One side has superhumans, laser beams, and comic book tech. The other side, doesn't. One side is defending, the other side isn't. One side has warships, the other is sending out tankers full of flammable, toxic, and otherwise useless waste in hope of dumping it into the water. It doesn't go well. The entire thing is a wreck, from start to finish. Aquaman comes by weekly to make sure all the toxic waste is simply dumped back into our universe, and then walks away. <br /> <br /> That's it. <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12952-accelerator","name":"Accelerator","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-03T03:31:14-08:00","id":1358578,"title":"","content":"Honestly we seem to have forgotten the Mad Scientist planning to invade the alternate Earth with no Superheros. Also I disagree with the other two posters- humanity has stupid moments, but we're not dumb. If that we're the case we wouldn't be the apex predators of Earth. Basic survival instincts would tell them not to fuck with the literal flying Superheroes that would squash them like flies. The realistic rundown is that they would prepare to fight the Mad Scientist. Nothing more, nothing less tbh. Even if they did mount expeditions in the alternate Earth, they would get their asses kicked by the other Superheroes on the other side. There is no comparative gain with all that risk involved. At best they'll probably send surveyor teams to better understand the alternate Earth, but thats it.<br /> <br /> Also to the OP of this thread, if you want to see a Superhero based game play Aberrant from the Trinity Continuum.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Jade Kingdom Warrior","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25523-shakanaka","name":"Shakanaka","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25523_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"951"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-03T07:09:10-08:00","id":1358616,"title":"","content":"We're... really not that great at acting smart as a collective; because we're not actually wired to run as multiple hundreds of millions of humans as on society.<br /> <br /> Also, the idea that you need to be not-stupid to become apex predators flies in the face of all the other apex predators not being as intelligent as us. The reason why we rose to dominance so quickly is a combination of two things: tool-use based adaptability and highly opportunistic expansionism. Most apex predators come from a long natural history of predators and happened to have the right combination of evolution, timing, and location to take over as a or the top predator in an ecosystem. We forged a rather unique and fast paced track by jumping from opportunistic omnivore foragers to high end predators in an incredibly short amount of time by evolutionary standards. <br /> <br /> The problem with how we did that, is that it's always put us on the road to unsustainable growth instead of equilibrium. But for most of our natural history, nature has kept us in check with disease and disaster. But we're overcoming those even faster than ever.<br /> <br /> The general point being, the whole portal situation hits all of our worst buttons. It's something new, thus we react with fear, territoriality, and aggression that we've' never shaken off from our pre-hominid ways, combined with our extreme curiosity, covetousness, and expansionist tendencies towards what such an event could mean. Combined with governmental systems that are very prone to misbehavior as they try to harness our negative qualities into positive ones, and we're primed to act destructively in response to such an event.<br /> <br /> We'd like to think we're more logical than that, but we're not. We'd love to think our intelligence is designed to win out in such as situation, but it isn't. Apex predators need to be able to avoid each other or things get ugly. We suck at avoiding conflict, because we engage in conflicts far too large for our brains to comprehend who is and isn't the strongest side and settle things quickly. We get in other predators' spaces, and generally speaking, we devastate them; often to our own detriment because we're not thinking about the disruption to the habitat that causes.<br /> <br /> So yes, as a whole, humanity tends to not act intelligently, and this scenario is designed to press all of our collective-stupid buttons.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-03T16:33:36-08:00","id":1358730,"title":"","content":"Heavy Arms is correct.<br /> <br /> &quot;Intelligent&quot; is perhaps a poor descriptor in this situation. Rather, humans are very &quot;Clever&quot;. Too clever for our own good, in many instances, because Clever =/= <i>Wise</i>.<br /> <br /> We love to think we've become wiser as a species, but that wisdom is inconsistent and fleeting. We're constantly having to re-learn the lessons of previous generations, and some lessons we <i>as a society</i> have not learned.<br /> <br /> The current state of affairs on the macro scale is built towards aggression, paranoia, and expansionism, because these things press all the most primal buttons of us humans.<br /> <br /> Opening up a portal to another world is just asking for trouble.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://archiveofourown.org/works/6956863/chapters/15862327\" target=\"_blank\">Magestuck: The Ascension</a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6156-bluecho","name":"Bluecho","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3871"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-03T23:04:52-08:00","id":1358774,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shakanaka</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1358159-what-s-a-realistic-reaction-to-superheroes?p=1358578#post1358578\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Also to the OP of this thread, if you want to see a Superhero based game play Aberrant from the Trinity Continuum.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, I'm afraid that the scenario in Aberrant is quite differet from the one here.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12952-accelerator","name":"Accelerator","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-03T23:07:28-08:00","id":1358775,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Bluecho</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1358159-what-s-a-realistic-reaction-to-superheroes?p=1358730#post1358730\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Heavy Arms is correct.<br /> <br /> &quot;Intelligent&quot; is perhaps a poor descriptor in this situation. Rather, humans are very &quot;Clever&quot;. Too clever for our own good, in many instances, because Clever =/= <i>Wise</i>.<br /> <br /> We love to think we've become wiser as a species, but that wisdom is inconsistent and fleeting. We're constantly having to re-learn the lessons of previous generations, and some lessons we <i>as a society</i> have not learned.<br /> <br /> The current state of affairs on the macro scale is built towards aggression, paranoia, and expansionism, because these things press all the most primal buttons of us humans.<br /> <br /> Opening up a portal to another world is just asking for trouble.</div> </div> </div> </div>So what you're saying, is that the presence of a portal to another world with superhumans who vastly outclass us and have superior tech means that we'll react with paranoia, fear, aggression and eventually some politician will start firing missiles?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12952-accelerator","name":"Accelerator","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-04T00:11:14-08:00","id":1358778,"title":"","content":"We're still different from common animals and other Apex Predators because we possess Sapience, rationality. Other animals are Clever too, but they aren't Wise. <i>HUMANS</i> are, thats what allows us to use tools and utilize basic kinship systems to further complex societies. It isn't rational to blindly try to make moves on a portal to another Earth more advanced than us with Superpowered entities that can smite whole contingents of an army. The heroes from the alternative reality are ultimately doing us a service since a Mad Scientist from their reality is attempting to take over OUR planet with technology too advanced to fight back against without Superpowered individuals who can combat it.<br /> <br /> Sure their maybe considerable advantage to get a foothold into the other Earth, but like I said before- there is too much risk involved. Modern warfare is a very complex form of warfare, it isn't easy to wage or fund with a high casualty rate. Why attempt to wage expeditions to gather resources at an alternate Earth where we know the same nations are present, but are more advanced? Gung-ho action only works when the appraising party is certain that they have a near unparalleled tactical advantage. The Alternate Earth Nations would probably stake out against us first, but at best everything would probably scare off into a interportal Cold-War.<br /> <br /> I do wonder how the economic markets in both alternate Earths would be effected if the portal stays even with the Mad Scientist is dealt with though.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Jade Kingdom Warrior","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25523-shakanaka","name":"Shakanaka","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25523_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"951"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-04T01:24:12-08:00","id":1358785,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shakanaka</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1358159-what-s-a-realistic-reaction-to-superheroes?p=1358778#post1358778\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I do wonder how the economic markets in both alternate Earths would be effected if the portal stays even with the Mad Scientist is dealt with though.</div> </div> </div> </div>Someone tries to sue superman for using the superman image.<br /> <br /> The DC comics sell like hotcakes. Marvel looks on in jealousy. <br /> <br /> Justice league members take a sabbatical on baseline earth. <br /> <br /> The DC animated show is required watching.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12952-accelerator","name":"Accelerator","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-04T01:34:40-08:00","id":1358788,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shakanaka</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1358159-what-s-a-realistic-reaction-to-superheroes?p=1358778#post1358778\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">We're still different from common animals and other Apex Predators because we possess Sapience, rationality.</div> </div> </div> </div>Sapience lacks any scientific standard of measurement. It is, in effect, a fancy word we use to justify calling ourselves special.<br /> <br /> That doesn't mean we don't have features as a species that are special in how they combined together (as far as we know), but there is precious little that we're actually better at than some other species; our lack of specialization is one of our strengths in that regard.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <i>HUMANS</i> are, thats what allows us to use tools and utilize basic kinship systems to further complex societies. </div> </div> </div>Other animals use tools and utilize kinship to for complex societies; ones far more efficient and logical in operations than ours manage. What does that make them? Are they sapient or just so clever there's no difference?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> It isn't rational... </div> </div> </div>Humans act irrationally all the time.<br /> <br /> Claiming human sapience is unique is irrational boasting where humans define something as good, and innately human, therefore making us good, with no rational metrics and definitions that can be tested to see if other species are sapie<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> It isn't rational to blindly try to make moves on a portal to another Earth more advanced than us with Superpowered entities that can smite whole contingents of an army. The heroes from the alternative reality are ultimately doing us a service since a Mad Scientist from their reality is attempting to take over OUR planet with technology too advanced to fight back against without Superpowered individuals who can combat it. </div> </div> </div>This is all assuming perfect knowledge of the situation we wouldn't have.<br /> <br /> What proof of any of this is there? There's just a portal, and a handful of beings that look like comic book heroes. How do we know they're not evil, the scientist is good, and they're just using those forms to trick us?<br /> <br /> We wouldn't. There's no reason to trust them at their word on any of it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-04T01:46:35-08:00","id":1358791,"title":"","content":"Of course you don't know. That's why you don't go in bumrushing them. <br /> <br /> Watch them. What do they do? Do they attack? Infiltrate? They have someone who appears to be superman and at least has some of his powers. Can they prove it? OK then. <br /> <br /> Not knowing anything breeds fear and caution. Not pure recklessness","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12952-accelerator","name":"Accelerator","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-04T01:58:16-08:00","id":1358795,"title":"","content":"Humans at large do have specialization. If we never did, the very first cities wouldn't never developed since we'd be stuck in the Neolithic age. Specialization is the very reason for the rise of the first city-states. We are more complex species on our Earth for the very reason we can devise technology. SOME animals can use basic tools, but mostly those animals are other primates like Gorillas or Monkeys of that sort, who we already had a common ancestor with. Tools alone don't progress society, technological systems of development applied in real time do.<br /> <br /> Thats what makes our societies complex. Humans have civilization, while animals ultimately don't. They can have complex pack or kinship animal societies, but they still have a baseline animal nature that isn't comparable to humans. They don't adapt as well humans do, don't have advanced morality, nor do they have advanced shelter (i.e villages, towns, and cities).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Jade Kingdom Warrior","edited":{"userid":25523,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25523-shakanaka","user":"Shakanaka","date":". 01-04-2020, 05:01 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25523-shakanaka","name":"Shakanaka","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25523_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"951"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-04T04:27:43-08:00","id":1358824,"title":"","content":"*is in utter confusion*","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12952-accelerator","name":"Accelerator","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-04T04:29:32-08:00","id":1358825,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Accelerator</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1358159-what-s-a-realistic-reaction-to-superheroes?p=1358791#post1358791\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Of course you don't know. That's why you don't go in bumrushing them.</div> </div> </div> </div>Any yet, humans have chosen to do so countless times in history, choosing initiative, surprise, and boldness over dispassion.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> They have someone who appears to be superman and at least has some of his powers. </div> </div> </div>All the more reasons not to wait. You can stun Superman with a nuke. Hard to do if he has a chance to get rid of all of ours before it's clear he's an enemy and we have no weapons left powerful enough to threaten him.<br /> <br /> Of course, this is why the JL shouldn't go through the portal in the first place. They should send a normal human diplomat to decrease potential tensions by not showing off that they've got the JL on their side if it can be avoided. You don't establish trust, or at least a stable line of communication, at the barrel of a gun even if you don't intend to use it. And Superman alone is a main battle tank being pointed at a child with a small stick. <br /> <br /> But the scenario was that the JL goes through without thinking about that (but hey, why should they be asked to be rational calm actors in all this too?).<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Not knowing anything breeds fear and caution. Not pure recklessness </div> </div> </div>Fear, literally, increases recklessness and decreases caution in our brains. Fear, as the saying goes, is the mind-killer. Clarity and caution only come after the urges of fear are mitigated.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shakanaka</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1358159-what-s-a-realistic-reaction-to-superheroes?p=1358795#post1358795\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Humans at large do have specialization.</div> </div> </div> </div>Let me clarify what I meant.<br /> <br /> Humans aren't specialized, as a species, to be extremely good at any given thing. We're not fast. We're not strong. We don't have efficient social structures. We don't even have the best memories or mental reflexes. Our biggest claim in this regard is that we're the best bipedal long range walkers. <br /> <br /> But our lack of specialization is a strength as well. Our tool use is so special to us precisely because it lets us overcome what our bodies can't manage. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> We are more complex species on our Earth for the very reason we can devise technology. </div> </div> </div>Technology doesn't make us a more complex species. Ant societies handle large collective complex systems... and most do so with no to little technology. But they don't need technology. They don't need to invent weapons, when they can breed soldier ants that are born with weapons. They don't need shovels or axes when worker ants are born with appendages for such activities. Etc.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> SOME animals can use basic tools, but mostly those animals are other primates like Gorillas or Monkeys of that sort, who we already had a common ancestor with. </div> </div> </div>Lots of animals can use basic tools, and most of them are neither primates nor monkeys. Though there are levels of tool use out there.<br /> <br /> Quite a large number of animals demonstrate rather complex tool <b>use</b> even if they do not naturally manufacture complex tools in the wild. Asian elephants are tool makers, that is, they don't just grab an item and use it, they modify it first which makes it technology, and repeatedly show that they are keen observers of human tools and learn what those tools are for rather quickly; even if most aren't things elephants can use because they're not designed to be operated by trunk. You can't keep them in a pen with electric fencing, because they'll disable electric fences after observing them. Without a single physics class, they figure out all they have to do is lean a heavy enough log or branch on them, and the fence shorts out and they can then push through the wires with ease.<br /> <br /> So, please, stop? I don't know what your background is regarding the study of animal intelligence, but you're not even demonstrating, &quot;I looked up what Wikipedia says,&quot; levels of knowledge on this stuff.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Tools alone don't progress society, technological systems of development applied in real time do. </div> </div> </div>This is... nonsense. Like, this sentence does not make sense. No single factor progresses society.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Humans have civilization, while animals ultimately don't. </div> </div> </div>Which is ultimately tautological. Like sapience, we define civilization in such a way that it excludes other animals for the sake of exclusion, rather than observation of natural phenomenon.<br /> <br /> Why don't ant colonies deserve to be called civilizations? Because they don't produce art? Because ants can't espouse ideologies to us? How is there a justification in anything other than starting with the premise that civilization is unique to humans and then fitting the definition to cater to that premise?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> ....but they still have a baseline animal nature that isn't comparable to humans. </div> </div> </div>And this fundamental conceit is the problem. We humans are animals, living according to our baseline animal nature.<br /> <br /> Do you not understand how hypocritical it is to be talking about the rational, logical, clear decision making humans do as a whole, while engaging in rhetoric based on the irrational and self serving desire for us to feel like we're special and above the other animals in some untouchable way?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-04T04:36:15-08:00","id":1358830,"title":"","content":"So basically, the moment the Justice League comes through, diplomacy's already turned dicy?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12952-accelerator","name":"Accelerator","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-04T05:14:46-08:00","id":1358841,"title":"","content":"Use of applied Technology does advance society. Its the simple reason why we got out the hunter-gatherer paleolithic age. We discovered to farm through the discovery that certain seeds can be deliberately nurtured to grow for consumption, instead of found and foraged for the next location. Humans have the most advanced social systems on the planet because we can enact on rational agreement to band together (social contract). Ants are merely complex by virtue of their instinct and pheromones to the hive, they aren't a civilization because they merely act out their biological imperative. Humans can establish law, while animals mostly only adhere to natural law. We can build extremely complex structures to inhabit in or use for a different purpose. Animals have different tiers of intelligence, so things like Elephants doing things you mentioned isn't surprising- but it can only go so far by simple matter of not needing it due to their nature and not having any use for it because they are tetrapods. At best they utilize sticks, but thats really it.<br /> <br /> Also to note we have writing systems, advanced forms of language, we can make weaponry to augment how we kill, we are ability to utilize natural resources in a more conducive way, etc.. Its not conceited to draw a logical conclusion that humans are different from animals, thus sapient. Just by acknowledging this doesn't remove us being animals in a technical sense, but the distinction is still obvious. To note by your definition of specialization in this argument, other animals aren't that specialized either by your logic. Not every animal has a long memory, strong, fast, or even have have fast mental reflexes. The biggest claim for most animals against humans is that they can process most foods raw without it being prepared and mostly need minimum shelter.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Our tool use is so special to us precisely because it lets us overcome what our bodies can't manage.</div> </div> </div> </div>You basically agree my argument with this. Humanities extensive tool use and development of complex society is what sets us apart from animals. With the first two sticks to make fire, that begat technology (the knowledge of paleo fire-starting). From there our mental faculties evolved higher than that of animals, which allowed us to out-compete all other species beside our own after agriculture was discovered. Thats what makes sapience, highly organized applied intelligence. Though even with that, never have I implied our base animal instincts are ever gone at all. It is still a facet of being animal regardless of any level of higher intellect.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Jade Kingdom Warrior","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25523-shakanaka","name":"Shakanaka","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25523_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"951"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-04T11:53:21-08:00","id":1358911,"title":"","content":"Diplomacy's dicey due to the Justice League in their own stories, in their own world. <a href=\"https://dcau.fandom.com/wiki/Task_Force_X\" target=\"_blank\">Task Force X</a> explicitly formed to stop superheroes and commit international crimes under the veil of costumed villainy. <a href=\"https://dcau.fandom.com/wiki/Project_Cadmus\" target=\"_blank\">Project Cadmus</a> was a secret government organization dedicated to stifling metahumans (often through human experimentation, which is where you got folks like Ace) and especially the Justice League, with one of its leaders a member of the Legion of Doom. It was a continuation from the Superman animated series, and started after an arc Superman literally came to Earth to conquer it as the commander of Darkseid's armies, and formed the Justice League to rebuild people's trust in him. Stepping over the wrong border, getting involved with political issues, and the criticism of them as a global non-governmental watchdog was a key part of their stories. Now you have them extending the same thing to another world, ours, where countries are assassinating high ranking officials via drones, meddling in elections, and gearing to start up a new nuclear arms race.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 01-04-2020, 02:57 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-04T15:15:24-08:00","id":1358943,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Accelerator</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1358159-what-s-a-realistic-reaction-to-superheroes?p=1358830#post1358830\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So basically, the moment the Justice League comes through, diplomacy's already turned dicy?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> At a minimum.<br /> <br /> First contact between human groups has always been dicey to start. There are so many ways things can go wrong, and horribly so, and we know it.<br /> <br /> It's actually in our nature. Human's aren't naturally equipped to care about &quot;humanity.&quot; We're equipped to care about &quot;us&quot; and not &quot;them.&quot; One could make a decent case that one of the defining cultural struggles of the past few centuries of human history, is the ideological battle over liberalism's attempt to get humans to put all other humans into the &quot;us&quot; box, and various anti-liberal political ideologies that promote the value keeping humans divided against each other. But that &quot;us vs. them&quot; mentality is our default state, and first contact between groups is always going to trigger &quot;us vs. them&quot; thinking. <br /> <br /> There's also, essentially, only two broad approaches to this. The first is the imperialist/colonialist approach of &quot;Exactly.&quot; The second is diplomacy, which requires a lot more work into investigating and studying before attempting contact to understand all the ways to decrease the tensions caused by the initial &quot;us vs. them&quot; that invariably occurs. <br /> <br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25523-shakanaka\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar25523_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"25523\" data-vbnamecard=\"25523\">Shakanaka</a> <br /> <br /> There's no point in trying to debate this, since you're unwilling to see past the ancient human indoctrination that we're &quot;special&quot; animals that are &quot;above&quot; or &quot;beyond,&quot; our fellow animals. Like countless before you, and unfortunately countless to come, you're unwilling to even engage with the idea that you're starting with a faulty premise and then doubling down on circular logic.<br /> <br /> And it's a shame, because nature and humans are all the more marvelous when you view us as part of nature instead of trying to manufacture justifications to say that we're distinct from it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-04T16:40:48-08:00","id":1358954,"title":"","content":"I guess cold War it is, then? As long as no one's too insane.<br /> <br /> The common people would love it, though? After all, they are superheroes from another dimension.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12952-accelerator","name":"Accelerator","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-04T17:29:50-08:00","id":1358965,"title":"","content":"The Cold War happened in a much more unique set of circumstances. Again, see all that stuff that's been said about more likely responses.<br /> <br /> And there is no &quot;common&quot; people here, since this would be a global situation, not just what consumers of American media might love. Even within those fans of American media, there are plenty of people that reject the idea of superheroes as a good thing even if they're well meaning individuals. The &quot;common&quot; people are sorely unprepared for the cultural upheaval a sudden and radical change to everything we know about the universe being upended would entail.<br /> <br /> Imagine, as a different hypothetical:<br /> <br /> Tomorrow, bright luminous beings descend from the sky. The perform a series of miracles that defy any explanation besides the supernatural. Then suddenly, everyone on Earth hears a voice in their head, this voice is soothing, but compelling, and we cannot help but believe it comes from a higher power to the core of our beings. It delivers the following message in a fashion that is perfectly understood. &quot;This is the Lord Almighty. I have decided to answer a question in hopes of saving you, my children. Baha'i is the one true faith.&quot; And then poof, all the bright beings go and the voice doesn't respond to any questions, prayers, or pleas.<br /> <br /> It would throw the world into utter chaos.<br /> <br /> Thinking that most people would be chill with a portal to another dimension opening up and super-beings coming through would be any different because it's &quot;science&quot; instead of religion baffles me.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-04T19:28:55-08:00","id":1358980,"title":"","content":"Well, ignoring the flaws in your analogy, what's your prediction on what'll happen?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12952-accelerator","name":"Accelerator","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-04T19:40:46-08:00","id":1358982,"title":"","content":"Well... ignoring the flaws in your post... oh, wait, I have nothing to say then.<br /> <br /> I don't have a specific prediction beyond general civil unrest on a massive scale, and a downward spiral as various powerful actors one-up each other in stupid decision making.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-04T21:56:33-08:00","id":1359000,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1358159-what-s-a-realistic-reaction-to-superheroes?p=1358982#post1358982\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well... ignoring the flaws in your post... oh, wait, I have nothing to say then.<br /> <br /> I don't have a specific prediction beyond general civil unrest on a massive scale, and a downward spiral as various powerful actors one-up each other in stupid decision making.</div> </div> </div> </div>Alright, fine. I'll answer you. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">Tomorrow, bright luminous beings descend from the sky. The perform a series of miracles that defy any explanation besides the supernatural. Then suddenly, everyone on Earth hears a voice in their head, this voice is soothing, but compelling, and we cannot help but believe it comes from a higher power to the core of our beings. It delivers the following message in a fashion that is perfectly understood. &quot;This is the Lord Almighty. I have decided to answer a question in hopes of saving you, my children. Baha'i is the one true faith.&quot; And then poof, all the bright beings go and the voice doesn't respond to any questions, prayers, or pleas.</span></span></span> </div> </div> </div>'Luminous beings descend from the sky. '<br /> <br /> Alright, fine, these are apparently angels. But in this scenario, this isn't angels. These are people who are literally talking to you, talking ot you, interacting with you. They can be touched, they can be felt, and they eat with you, like literal people. They are not 'luminous beings descend from the sky and don't tell you anything'. Yes, they're going to answer your questions. In this case, there's going to be a fuck load more information we get, considering that they actually answer our questions. <br /> <br /> 'This is the Lord Almighty'. <br /> <br /> Yeah, this isn't happening. The Lord Almighty speaking is vastly different from people from fictional stories popping up in real life. For one thing, there's the whole theology issue. And secondly, he isn't talking spirituality. A fictional story suddenly turning out to be true is going to rock human existence, but it certainly isn't going to completely upend human spirituality like a mass telepathic message talking about the one true faith. <br /> <br /> You know what? This was a waste of time.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12952-accelerator","name":"Accelerator","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-04T23:34:20-08:00","id":1359015,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1358159-what-s-a-realistic-reaction-to-superheroes?p=1358965#post1358965\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Even within those fans of American media, there are plenty of people that reject the idea of superheroes as a good thing even if they're well meaning individuals.</div> </div> </div> </div>I mean, supers <i>could</i> be good, but powered individuals working to improve society from <i>within</i> the system (and working to solve systemic problems, rather than the ones you can just punch) would nearly always be better.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12952-accelerator\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"12952\" data-vbnamecard=\"12952\">Accelerator</a> also, the DCAU being real would present at least as many theological problems as Baha\u2019i God announcing himself would. There are gods in the DC Universe, from Hades and Hephaestus to Darkseid and Dr. Manhattan. <br /> <br /> And, if God created a whole separate universe with supermen running around and made it possible within the laws of physics for them to visit us, and then didn\u2019t warn us about it, he\u2019d have a hell of a lot to answer for.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":177,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","user":"TheCountAlucard","date":". 01-05-2020, 02:58 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-04T23:38:23-08:00","id":1359018,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1358159-what-s-a-realistic-reaction-to-superheroes?p=1359015#post1359015\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I mean, supers <i>could</i> be good, but powered individuals working To improve society from <i>within</i> the system (and working to solve systemic problems, rather than the ones you can just punch) would nearly always be better.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12952-accelerator\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"12952\" data-vbnamecard=\"12952\">Accelerator</a> also, the DCAU being real would present at least as many theological problems as Baha\u2019i God announcing himself would. There are gods in the DC Universe, from Hades and Hephaestus to Darkseid and Dr. Manhattan.<br /> <br /> And, if God created a whole separate universe with supermen running around and made it possible within the laws of physics for them to visit us, he\u2019d have a hell of a lot to answer for.</div> </div> </div> </div>Maybe this was a dumb question to ask.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12952-accelerator","name":"Accelerator","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-04T23:56:33-08:00","id":1359019,"title":"","content":"Just because you don\u2019t like the answer, doesn\u2019t make it a dumb question.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-05T01:00:48-08:00","id":1359033,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Accelerator</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1358159-what-s-a-realistic-reaction-to-superheroes?p=1359000#post1359000\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You know what? This was a waste of time.</div> </div> </div> </div>Because you're nitpicking differences in situations that were never presented as identical to avoid looking at the similarities.<br /> <br /> Though I'd point out that many atheists would completely describe my scenario as, &quot;...people from fictional stories popping up in real life.&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-05T03:23:23-08:00","id":1359040,"title":"","content":"He\u2019s been temp-banned.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-05T04:29:42-08:00","id":1359045,"title":"","content":"Yeah, I saw that after I posted.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-05T11:08:40-08:00","id":1359099,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1358159-what-s-a-realistic-reaction-to-superheroes?p=1359015#post1359015\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">also, the DCAU being real would present at least as many theological problems as Baha\u2019i God announcing himself would. There are gods in the DC Universe, from Hades and Hephaestus to Darkseid and Dr. Manhattan.<br /> <br /> And, if God created a whole separate universe with supermen running around and made it possible within the laws of physics for them to visit us, and then didn\u2019t warn us about it, he\u2019d have a hell of a lot to answer for.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes. There's literal Angels and Lucifer and the whole Judeo-Christian population roaming around up there. I was more focused on the government side but I have to imagine the reaction to 'Your religion is demonstrably true, through that portal' would not be a reserved one.<br /> <br /> Sort of like the uh 'stairway to heaven' idea, I think they made a movie about it. If someone finds a stairway that seems to lead to nowhere, and people don't actually return from it, but they're able to visit their loved ones (once) in dreams afterward and tell them that they're in heaven or paradise or some other eternally pleasing afterlife. Would you have a rush of people heading towards it? The governments of the world, needing masses, would probably try to stop it from being used. What would the stances on organized religion be, when faced with losing their organization at an easy and direct answer? Would governments of the world try to come up with a 'When you're retired, or physically ailing, you can go through' law?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-28T00:39:17-08:00","id":1363754,"title":"","content":"The answer is quite simple. It will never happen so you will never know what reaction should be realistic","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25919-myrtlerankind","name":"myrtlerankind","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}